{"id":"word:hebrew:H3526","type":"word","title":"כָּבַס","subtitle":"H3526 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"to trample ; hence, to wash (properly, by stamping with the feet), whether literal (including the fulling process) or figurative","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to כָּבַס (H3526) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: v.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 51 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"כָּבַס (kâbaç) means to trample ; hence, to wash (properly, by stamping with the feet), whether literal (including the fulling process) or figurative First listed occurrence: 2Kgs 18 17."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"כָּבַס","transliteration":"kâbaç","pronunciation":"kaw-bas'","strong":"H3526","lemmaId":"hebrew:H3526","partOfSpeech":"v","forms":["יְכַבֵּ֧ס","יְכַבֵּ֥ס","וְ/כִבֶּ֧ס","כוֹבֵֽס","יְכַבֵּ֣ס"],"morphs":[["HVpi3ms",17],["HC/Vpq3ms",12],["HVqrmsa",3],["HC/Vpq3cp",3],["HVpp3ms",2],["HC/Vpw3mp",2],["HVpi2ms",2],["HVuc",2],["HC/VPq3ms",2],["HVpi2fs",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"to trample ; hence, to wash (properly, by stamping with the feet), whether literal (including the fulling process) or figurative","usage":"fuller, wash(-ing).","full":"H3526. kabas [ כָּבַס ] 51 verb (tread), wash (Late Hebrew id. ; Phoenician כבס as participle; Assyrian kabâsu , tread ( down ), subjugate , kibšu , step, path , Dl HWB ) — Qal Participle only כוֺבֵס שְׂדֵה מְסִלַּת highway of fuller's (= treader's, washer's ) field Isa 7:3 ; 36:2 = 2Kin 18:17 . Pi`el Perfect וְכִּבֶּס consecutive Lev 13:6 11 t.; כִּבֵּס Gen 49:11 ; 2Sam 19:25 , etc.; Imperfect יְכַבֵּס Lev 11:25 16 t.; 2 masculine singular suffix תְּכַבְּסֵנִי Psa 51:9 , etc.; Imperative suffix כַּבְּסֵנִי 51:4 ; feminine singular כַּבְּסִי Jer 4:14 ; Participle plural מְכַבְּסִים Mal 3:2 ; &#8212; 1 wash garments (i.e. by treading ) Exod 19:10 , 14 (E), 2Sam 19:25 ; figurative of Judah Gen 49:11 ; elsewhere chiefly P: Lev 6:20 ; 11:25 , 28 ; 13:6 , 34 ; 15:11 ; Num 8:9 +; || רָחץ (which = wash person ) Lev 14:8-9 , 15:5-6 , 7 , 8 , 10 , 11 + ( ׳כ in Leviticus 27 t., || ׳ר 15t.; in Numbers 8 t., || ׳ר 3t.); Participle = fuller (compare Qal), only מְכ ׳בֹּרִית Mal 3:2 . 2 wash person, only in poetry and figurative בַּנֶּתֶר תְּכַבְּסִי אִם Jer 2:22 ; לִבֵךְ מֵרָעָה כַּבְּסִי 4:14 ; with suffix Psa 51:4 (|| טהר ; + מֵעָוֺן ); 51:9 (|| חִטֵּא ). Pu`al Perfect וְכֻבַּס consecutive Lev 13:58 ; 15:17 be washed , of garment. Hothpa`al (Ges § 54 , 3) Infinitive אֶתהַֿנֶּגַע הֻכַּבֵּס אַחֲרֵי Lev 13:55 after the plague is washed out , so 13:56 .","rootNote":"a primitive root;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"2Kgs 18 17","keyReferences":["2Kgs 18 17","2Sam 19 25","Exod 19 10","Exod 19 14","Gen 49 11","Isa 7 3","Isa 36 2","Jer 2 22"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":51,"occurrences":[{"reference":"2Kgs 18 17","book":"2Kgs","chapter":18,"verse":17,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"כוֹבֵֽס","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqrmsa"},{"reference":"2Sam 19 25","book":"2Sam","chapter":19,"verse":25,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"כִבֵּ֔ס","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVpp3ms"},{"reference":"Exod 19 10","book":"Exod","chapter":19,"verse":10,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וְ/כִבְּס֖וּ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vpq3cp"},{"reference":"Exod 19 14","book":"Exod","chapter":19,"verse":14,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַֽ/יְכַבְּס֖וּ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vpw3mp"},{"reference":"Gen 49 11","book":"Gen","chapter":49,"verse":11,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"כִּבֵּ֤ס","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVpp3ms"},{"reference":"Isa 7 3","book":"Isa","chapter":7,"verse":3,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"כוֹבֵֽס","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqrmsa"},{"reference":"Isa 36 2","book":"Isa","chapter":36,"verse":2,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"כוֹבֵֽס","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqrmsa"},{"referen